strategy:
A deterministic beam search over the timestamp-sorted log builds an initial joint hypothesis of event assignments and session states, scored by a graded cost model for missing events, jitter, duplicates and crashes. The cost is split into a sum of independent per-session replay costs. An improvement loop then alternates three neighbourhoods and accepts only moves that lower the total cost:
- single-event moves and swaps;
- block moves (contiguous runs and suffix exchanges);
- large-neighbourhood ruin-and-recreate, which clears all anonymous events in a time window on one node and re-inserts them greedily by exact replay-cost delta, forward, backward and in regret order.

